<item>
            <title>[LU-20574] utils: tunefs.lustre --quota silently discards the options stored in the LDD</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20574</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;tunefs.lustre --quota enables quota accounting on the backing filesystem and then returns immediately, so osd_write_ldd() is never reached:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
  &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* Enable quota accounting */&lt;/span&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (mop.mo_flags &amp;amp; MO_QUOTA) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ret = osd_enable_quota(&amp;amp;mop);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;goto&lt;/span&gt; out;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; }write:#endif &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* !TUNEFS */&lt;/span&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;/* Write our config files */&lt;/span&gt;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ret = osd_write_ldd(&amp;amp;mop);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (ret != 0) {
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; fatal();
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; fprintf(stderr, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;failed to write local files\n&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;goto&lt;/span&gt; out;
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; }
out:
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; osd_fini();
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ret2 = loop_cleanup(&amp;amp;mop);
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (ret == 0)
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ret = ret2; &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reproduce steps:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
# tunefs.lustre --quota --comment=test /dev/nvme1n1
checking &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; existing Lustre data: found&#160; &#160;Read previous values:
Device: &#160; &#160; /dev/nvme1n1
Target: &#160; &#160; test-MDT0001
Index: &#160; &#160; &#160;1
Lustre FS: &#160;test
Mount type: ldiskfs
Flags: &#160; &#160; &#160;0x1
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; (MDT )
Persistent mount opts: user_xattr,errors=remount-ro
Parameters: mgsnode=172.16.46.134@tcp
&#160; &#160;Permanent disk data:
Device: &#160; &#160; /dev/nvme1n1
Target: &#160; &#160; test-MDT0001
Index: &#160; &#160; &#160;1
Lustre FS: &#160;test
Mount type: ldiskfs
Flags: &#160; &#160; &#160;0x1
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; (MDT )
Persistent mount opts: user_xattr,errors=remount-ro
Parameters: mgsnode=172.16.46.134@tcp
Comment: testQuota feature is already enabled.
# tunefs.lustre /dev/nvme1n1
checking &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; existing Lustre data: found&#160; &#160;Read previous values:
Device: &#160; &#160; /dev/nvme1n1
Target: &#160; &#160; test-MDT0001
Index: &#160; &#160; &#160;1
Lustre FS: &#160;test
Mount type: ldiskfs
Flags: &#160; &#160; &#160;0x1
&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; (MDT )
Persistent mount opts: user_xattr,errors=remount-ro
Parameters: mgsnode=172.16.46.134@tcpexiting because there is no change. &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
